{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YEVfisQAp1qYGZMKA9mQCs","type":"tool_result","content":"160:## *\"You don't give Kubernetes orders. You file a declaration.\"*\n169:## Attention Budget\n200:## 🧭 Soundings\n249:## Why This Chapter Matters\n261:## What You'll Learn\n276:## §1 — ⚪ You File a Declaration\n296:### Three ways to manage an object\n334:## §2 — ⚪ The Anatomy of a Record\n340:### The four fields\n366:### The two halves of identity\n403:### The two fields that matter most\n423:### What actually happens when you apply\n459:## ☆ Taking Your Bearings #1: The Declarative Frame and Object Anatomy\n518:## §3 — 🔵 Where a Name Lives\n530:### The correction most guides skip\n536:### Not everything lives in a namespace\n569:### The four initial namespaces\n594:## §4 — 🔵 Configuration Kept Outside the Image\n604:### ConfigMap\n624:### Secret\n632:### Base64 is not a lock\n656:### Types of Secret\n679:### Side by side\n726:## ☆ Taking Your Bearings #2: Scoping and Configuration Objects\n777:## §5 — 🔵 The Universal Join\n797:### The label selector\n827:### The bridge to what you will actually see\n843:### Annotations, by contrast\n883:## ☆ Taking Your Bearings #3: Labels, Selectors, and Annotations\n940:## §6 — 🟡 A Declaration, Not an Order\n975:### ☀️ Zenith\n989:### The honest correction\n999:## Exam Alert! 🚨\n1030:## Practice Questions\n1191:### Answers and Explanations\n1295:## Chapter Summary\n1321:## 🏆 Safe Harbor\n1329:## The Voyage Ahead","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0d80b48-2829-470e-8f77-7da3952fe035","uuid":"1dee2cc8-0c27-47f1-b5c6-ba32ea8e71e3","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:18:07.462Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"160:## *\"You don't give Kubernetes orders. You file a declaration.\"*\n169:## Attention Budget\n200:## 🧭 Soundings\n249:## Why This Chapter Matters\n261:## What You'll Learn\n276:## §1 — ⚪ You File a Declaration\n296:### Three ways to manage an object\n334:## §2 — ⚪ The Anatomy of